   "notes": "Described the base Mixtral 8x7B (the Instruct model shares the architecture). Norm type, pre-norm placement and RoPE are marked inherited from Mistral 7B via the explicit inheritance sentence. RoPE theta, pairing, norm eps, biases and tied embeddings are not restated in the paper and are left not_stated. Mistral 7B's sliding-window attention is explicitly overridden: the paper says Mixtral uses fully dense 32k context, so attention is exact with window 0. Gating is a softmax over the top-2 logits only (non-selected logits set to -inf), i.e. renorm. Projection widths are not given beyond the table and follow from heads x head_dim."
